    "done_when": "The inventory /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/fsa-renderer-call-sites-inside-wall.md (reviewed 92) lists 78 unguarded calls in 36 files and specifies the rule. tests/renderer_wall_scan.py is an importable module with a function that takes source paths and returns one record per unguarded call (file, line, call kind), and a command-line entry that prints those records and exits nonzero when any exist. It flags Axes.tricontour, tricontourf, contour and contourf fed by scattered coordinates, and draw_flux_contours calls fed by _raster_field, LinearNDInterpolator, griddata or a scattered receipt, unless the call goes through draw_scattered_contours with a wall, passes wall= to draw_flux_contours, or uses a raster already blanked through inside_wall_units. tests/test_renderer_wall_scan.py proves it against the inventory controls: it flags plasma_cell_fixed_point_attribution.py:424 and sol_ledger_current_census.py:415 by file and line, passes closed-forms/render.py:52 and contour_tree_explanatory_figure.py:359, does not flag the post-filtered probe at plasma_cell_trip_panels.py:406, and when run over benchmarks/ and docs/figures/ at this base reports exactly the 78 sites of the inventory, a count that the test asserts and the report reconciles site by site. No renderer is edited. Gate: JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_renderer_wall_scan.py passes with zero added failures against the base.",
